  },
  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "The derivative is the instantaneous rate of change: the slope of the tangent line, defined as a limit of average rates.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "Below, \\( f(x)=\\tfrac{x^{3}}{3}-x \\) is in indigo and its derivative \\( f'(x)=x^{2}-1 \\) in amber. Slide \\( x \\): the <em>height</em> of the amber curve equals the <em>slope</em> of the indigo one.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "explorer",
        "canvasId": "apDerivCanvas",
        "title": {
          "en": "⊙ Explorer · A function and its derivative",
          "ar": null
        },
        "ariaLabel": {
          "en": "A cubic function and its derivative plotted on the same axes",
          "ar": null
        },
        "dataPanel": {
          "btnId": "apDerivDataBtn",
          "panelId": "apDerivDataPanel",
          "descId": "apDerivDataDesc",
          "rowsId": "apDerivDataRows",
          "caption": {
            "en": "Sampled points on f(x) and its derivative f′(x)",
            "ar": null
          },
          "columns": [
            {
              "en": "x",
              "ar": null
            },
            {
              "en": "f(x)",
              "ar": null
            },
            {
              "en": "f′(x)",
              "ar": null
            }
          ]
        },
        "controls": [
          {
            "id": "apDerivX",
            "label": {
              "en": "Point <b>x =</b>",
              "ar": null
            },
            "min": -2.5,
            "max": 2.5,
            "value": 1,
            "step": 0.1,
            "valueDisplayId": "apDerivXV",
            "ariaLabel": {
              "en": "Point x",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ],
        "readouts": [
          {
            "id": "apDerivFx",
            "label": {
              "en": "f(x)",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": "—",
            "colorClass": "indigo"
          },
          {
            "id": "apDerivSlope",
            "label": {
              "en": "f '(x) = slope",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": "—",
            "colorClass": "amber"
          }
        ],
        "note": {
          "en": "Where \\( f \\) is flat (\\( f'=0 \\)) the amber curve crosses zero — those are the max and min of \\( f \\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "thm",
        "label": {
          "en": "▲ Reference — The derivative",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>\\( f'(x)=\\displaystyle\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x)}{h} \\). From it follow the power, constant-multiple, sum, product, and quotient rules.</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "figure",
        "figure": {
          "type": "fn",
          "title": "Secant Line Approaching Tangent Line",
          "xrange": [
            -1,
            4
          ],
          "yrange": [
            -1,
            9
          ],
          "fns": [
            {
              "fn": "x^2",
              "color": "var(--fig-indigo-2)",
              "label": "f(x) = x²"
            },
            {
              "fn": "2*x - 1",
              "color": "var(--fig-amber)",
              "label": "Tangent: y = 2x - 1"
            },
            {
              "fn": "3*x - 2",
              "color": "var(--fig-teal)",
              "label": "Secant (x=1 to x=2)"
            }
          ],
          "points": [
            {
              "x": 1,
              "y": 1,
              "label": "P(1,1)"
            },
            {
              "x": 2,
              "y": 4,
              "label": "Q(2,4)"
            }
          ]
        },
        "caption": {
          "en": "As the point \\( Q(x+h, f(x+h)) \\) slides toward \\( P(x, f(x)) \\) (letting \\( h \\to 0 \\)), the slope of the secant line approaches the slope of the tangent line: \\( f'(1) = 2 \\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Definition",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\lim_{h\\to0}\\dfrac{f(x+h)-f(x)}{h} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Power rule",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\dfrac{d}{dx}x^{n}=nx^{n-1} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Product",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( (uv)'=u'v+uv' \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Quotient",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\left(\\dfrac{u}{v}\\right)'=\\dfrac{u'v-uv'}{v^{2}} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 2.A",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Differentiate \\( f(x)=3x^{4}-2x \\).</p>\\[ f'(x)=12x^{3}-2. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example — Differentiability from the limit definition",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Find \\(f'(x)\\) for \\(f(x)=x^2-3x\\) using the limit definition.</p>\\[f'(x)=\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac{(x+h)^2-3(x+h)-(x^2-3x)}{h}=\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac{2xh+h^2-3h}{h}=\\lim_{h\\to0}(2x+h-3)=2x-3.\\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "warn",
        "label": {
          "en": "⚠ Common traps — Quotient rule order & non-differentiability",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p><strong>Quotient rule order matters:</strong> \\( \\left(\\dfrac{u}{v}\\right)' = \\dfrac{u'v - uv'}{v^2} \\). Reversing the numerator to \\( uv' - u'v \\) introduces a false negative sign across the entire derivative.</p><p><strong>Continuity does not imply differentiability:</strong> A function can be continuous everywhere but fail to be differentiable at sharp corners (e.g. \\( f(x) = |x| \\) at \\( x=0 \\)), cusps (\\( x^{2/3} \\) at \\( x=0 \\)), or vertical tangents (\\( x^{1/3} \\) at \\( x=0 \\)).</p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0\"><strong>Power rule on fractions:</strong> When differentiating \\( f(x) = \\dfrac{1}{x^3} \\), write it as \\( x^{-3} \\) first: \\( f'(x) = -3x^{-4} = -\\dfrac{3}{x^4} \\). Do not simply differentiate the denominator in place!</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "Differentiate \\(y=x^4\\sin x\\). (Product rule)",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "\\(y'=4x^3\\sin x+x^4\\cos x\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "Find the derivative of \\(f(x) = \\dfrac{2x - 1}{x^2 + 3}\\) using the quotient rule.",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "<p>Apply the quotient rule \\(\\left(\\frac{u}{v}\\right)' = \\frac{u'v - uv'}{v^2}\\):</p>\\[ f'(x) = \\frac{2(x^2 + 3) - (2x - 1)(2x)}{(x^2 + 3)^2} = \\frac{2x^2 + 6 - (4x^2 - 2x)}{(x^2 + 3)^2} = \\frac{-2x^2 + 2x + 6}{(x^2 + 3)^2}. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "quizWidget": {
    "domains": [
      "Definition of the Derivative",
      "Differentiation Rules"
    ]
  }
}
